  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most critical uncertainty is establishing a performance baseline against which all design choices (multimodal fusion, multiprofile aggregation, learned encoders) can be meaningfully evaluated. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most standard configuration in the space: it uses a well-understood linear dimensionality reduction (PCA), a single profile (avoiding aggregation confounds), and no image modality. This gives a clean floor performance. Any future gain from adding images, switching to learned encoders (scvi, scgpt), multiprofile aggregation, or fusion strategies can then be attributed to those specific design decisions. Starting here maximizes the interpretability of every subsequent experiment under a limited budget, since it anchors the entire search to a well-defined reference point."
}

